/*
 * In eva_main such a copy reads a fully initialized shadow of the input. Eva does not relate fuzz_len
 * to the initialized prefix of input_buf, so a copy from input_buf itself would leave every
 * argument possibly uninitialized, even behind the harness's own length guard. The guard is harness
 * code, so the copied bytes are input bytes: any initialized value. A pointer the target receives
 * into the input still points into input_buf, where a read past input_len is an alarm.
 */
